#!/usr/bin/env python
"""The real-scale space set's maps (space_epic, 2026-11-08). Nothing downloaded: the Earth is drawn from continent outlines written by hand
(lon, lat in degrees, a few dozen points each), roughened with fractal noise, coloured by latitude, dryness and named regions; its night side
is ~230 cities with satellite towns and roads. The Moon's maria are placed where they are. Jupiter, Saturn and the rings are 1D profiles of
their real bands (latitude or radius to colour); the shader (MVSpaceFar.shader) adds the turbulence, storms and craters.
   uv run --no-project --with numpy --with pillow python Director/tools/space_tex.py [earth lights moon bands rings]
Writes Assets/MusicVideo/Props/Space/<name>.png."""
